    "7:9–16 — Patriarchs, jealous of Joseph, sell him. God is with him in Egypt. Famine. A second visit. Joseph made known to his brethren. Jacob down to Egypt, death, burial at Shechem. Stephen's geography is slightly compressed against Genesis 50 / Joshua 24 — a real stitch readers notice. The load is not a land-survey. It is that the brothers rejected the one God meant to save them by, the first time.",
    "7:17–29 — The promise draws near. A new king. Moses born, fair, learned in Egypt, mighty in words and deeds. At forty he visits his brethren, slays the Egyptian, and assumes they will understand God by his hand is giving deliverance. They do not. 'Who made thee a ruler and a judge?' He flees to Midian. The pattern: a delivered-and-rejected deliverer. Stephen is not wandering. He is building a mold.",
