    "8:5–8 — Philip goes down to Samaria and preaches Christ. Crowds give heed, seeing signs. Unclean spirits cry out; many palsied and lame are healed. Great joy in that city. John 4 already had a Samaritan town asking Jesus to stay. Acts 8 is that crack opening under persecution.",
    "8:9–25 — Simon the sorcerer had bewitched the people, giving out that himself was some great one. They said, This man is the great power of God. He believes, is baptized, continues with Philip, wondering. Apostles in Jerusalem hear that Samaria has received the word. They send Peter and John. The Spirit has not yet fallen; they have only been baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus. Hands laid, they receive the Holy Ghost. Simon offers money for the power of laying on hands. Peter: thy money perish with thee. The gift of God is not purchased. Thy heart is not right. Repent. Simon asks them to pray that none of these things come on him. They preach back toward Jerusalem, in many Samaritan villages. The delay of the Spirit here is a live puzzle. Luke wants apostolic hands across an old Jew-Samaritan wound before the next city is claimed.",
