    "12:6–11 — The night before Herod would bring him out, Peter sleeps between two soldiers, bound with two chains, keepers before the door. A light, an angel, a side struck, chains off. Gird thyself, bind on sandals, cast thy garment, follow. He thinks he sees a vision. Through the first and second ward, iron gate opening of its own accord, one street, and the angel departs. 'Now I know of a surety, that the Lord hath sent his angel, and hath delivered me out of the hand of Herod, and from all the expectation of the people of the Jews.' Psalm 34:7 is older language for this kind of night.",
